---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';

const canonicalUrl = 'https://handheldsettings.com/legion-go-settings/no-mans-sky/';
const title = "No Man's Sky Legion Go settings: 800p/30 baseline — Handheld Settings Lab";
const description = "Start No Man's Sky on the original Lenovo Legion Go with a cautious 800p/30 FPS baseline, a 40 FPS test path, planet and space-flight checks, and 15GB storage planning.";
const image = '/assets/games/no-mans-sky-header.jpg';

const sources = [
  { label: "Steam: No Man's Sky requirements, features, controller support, and official media", url: 'https://store.steampowered.com/app/275850/No_Mans_Sky/' },
  { label: 'Steam app-details API: current public product data for app 275850', url: 'https://store.steampowered.com/api/appdetails?appids=275850&cc=us&l=en' },
  { label: "Hello Games: official No Man's Sky site", url: 'https://www.nomanssky.com/' },
  { label: "Hello Games: official No Man's Sky release log", url: 'https://www.nomanssky.com/release-log/' },
  { label: 'Lenovo PSREF: original Legion Go 8APU1 specifications', url: 'https://psref.lenovo.com/Product/Legion/Legion_Go_8APU1' }
];

const faqs = [
  {
    question: "What No Man's Sky settings should I use on Legion Go?",
    answer: 'Start at 1280×800, a 30 FPS cap, and the Standard preset. Set shadows, reflections, volumetrics, and planet quality to Standard for the first pass, and use a Quality-class in-game upscaler if the current build offers one. Test a busy planetary base, low flight, and a space encounter before raising settings. This is a cautious editorial baseline, not a personally measured result.'
  },
  {
    question: "Can Legion Go run No Man's Sky at 40 FPS?",
    answer: 'Use 40 FPS as a second test, not a guarantee. First validate 800p/30 across a dense planet, base, weather, atmosphere transition, and space combat. If those passes retain headroom, change only the cap and repeat them. Procedural worlds, settlements, multiplayer activity, patches, power, drivers, and thermals can change the outcome.'
  },
  {
    question: "Should I use 800p, 1200p, or 1600p for No Man's Sky on Legion Go?",
    answer: 'Start at 800p because it preserves the panel’s 16:10 shape and gives planet rendering more headroom. Try 1200p only after the same demanding route is stable, changing no other control. Native 1600p is better treated as an experiment for unusually light scenes than as the default performance baseline.'
  },
  {
    question: "Which No Man's Sky settings should I lower first?",
    answer: 'Reduce shadows, reflections, volumetric quality, planet quality, base complexity, and animation quality before making the interface or nearby textures unnecessarily soft. Change one setting at a time and repeat the same planet-to-space route because different worlds expose different limits.'
  },
  {
    question: "How much storage does No Man's Sky need?",
    answer: 'Steam currently lists 15GB of available space. Leave additional free room for game updates, shader data, saves, screenshots, recordings, and Windows temporary files rather than planning to fill the drive to exactly 15GB.'
  },
  {
    question: "Were these No Man's Sky Legion Go settings personally benchmarked?",
    answer: 'No. Handheld Settings Lab checked current Valve, Hello Games, and Lenovo public sources but did not personally benchmark the current game, save, planet, Windows build, driver, firmware, Legion Space version, battery, or thermals. The page provides a reproducible starting workflow without inventing an FPS or runtime result.'
  }
];

const jsonLd = [
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'TechArticle',
    headline: "No Man's Sky Legion Go settings: 800p/30 FPS baseline",
    description,
    image: `https://handheldsettings.com${image}`,
    url: canonicalUrl,
    datePublished: '2026-08-16',
    dateModified: '2026-08-16',
    author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Handheld Settings Lab' },
    publisher: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'Handheld Settings Lab', url: 'https://handheldsettings.com/' },
    about: ["No Man's Sky", 'Lenovo Legion Go', 'game settings', 'frame rate', 'handheld PC']
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
    itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'Home', item: 'https://handheldsettings.com/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'Legion Go settings', item: 'https://handheldsettings.com/legion-go-settings/' },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 3, name: "No Man's Sky settings", item: canonicalUrl }
    ]
  },
  {
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'FAQPage',
    mainEntity: faqs.map(faq => ({
      '@type': 'Question',
      name: faq.question,
      acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: faq.answer }
    }))
  }
];
---
<Base title={title} description={description} image={image} jsonLd={jsonLd}>
  <article class="wrap article">
    <span class="eyebrow">Legion Go settings · Baseline published August 2026</span>
    <h1>No Man's Sky Legion Go settings: start at 800p and 30 FPS</h1>
    <p class="lede muted">No Man's Sky can move from a quiet interior to procedural terrain, dense flora, weather, settlements, atmosphere transitions, freighter spaces, and multiplayer activity. This original Legion Go workflow starts at a cautious 800p/30 Standard profile, then tests 40 FPS only after the same planet-to-space route passes. It is official-source-informed guidance—not a personally tested benchmark.</p>

    <figure class="game-hero">
      <img src={image} alt="Official No Man's Sky Steam header artwork showing a traveler overlooking an alien landscape" width="460" height="215" />
      <figcaption class="media-credit">Official No Man's Sky Steam store header image, saved locally from <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/275850/No_Mans_Sky/" target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">Hello Games' Steam store page</a>. Artwork and trademarks belong to Hello Games; editorial use does not imply endorsement.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div class="settings-panel">
      <section class="card"><h3>Safe first target</h3><div class="stat">800p / 30</div><p class="muted">Baseline to validate, not a lock guarantee</p></section>
      <section class="card"><h3>Starting preset</h3><div class="stat">Standard</div><p class="muted">Raise clarity after planet-to-space testing</p></section>
      <section class="card"><h3>Second target</h3><div class="stat">40 FPS</div><p class="muted">Test only after the 30 FPS route passes</p></section>
      <section class="card"><h3>Storage floor</h3><div class="stat">15GB</div><p class="muted">Current Steam requirement; leave update room</p></section>
    </div>

    <div class="callout"><strong>One planet is not the benchmark:</strong> procedural terrain, weather, base complexity, NPCs, multiplayer, and patches can produce a different workload. Save the exact portal/base location or route used, then include low flight, an atmosphere transition, and space combat in every comparison.</div>

    <h2>Recommended No Man's Sky Legion Go baseline</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Control</th><th>Start here</th><th>Reason</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Legion Go power mode</td><td>Performance-class profile</td><td>Creates a repeatable first condition. Record whether the device is on battery or connected directly to a compatible charger.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Display refresh rate</td><td>60Hz for the 30 FPS baseline</td><td>Provides a simple first pacing relationship. Record the refresh state again if testing a different cap later.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Display mode / resolution</td><td>Fullscreen / 1280×800</td><td>Preserves the panel's 16:10 shape while reducing render load substantially from native 2560×1600.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Frame-rate cap</td><td>30 FPS first</td><td>Prioritizes consistency through terrain streaming, storms, bases, and transitions. Test 40 FPS only after this profile passes.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Graphics preset</td><td>Standard</td><td>Provides a cautious diagnostic floor without pretending the Low/Standard profile is a measured requirement for every world.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Anti-aliasing / upscaling</td><td>Quality-class in-game mode, if offered</td><td>Starts from the clearer reconstruction option. Use the current menu's normal in-game control and avoid stacking it with driver scaling.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Texture quality</td><td>Standard, then raise carefully</td><td>Nearby materials matter in exploration, but the handheld uses shared memory. Watch texture streaming and traversal hitches before raising it.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Shadow quality / reflections</td><td>Standard</td><td>Protects headroom in moving sunlight, water, ships, interiors, and weather before sacrificing interface clarity.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Volumetric quality</td><td>Standard</td><td>Reduces the cost of clouds, fog, storms, and atmosphere transitions in the initial test.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Planet quality</td><td>Standard</td><td>Limits terrain detail and streaming pressure while testing low flight and fast surface traversal.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Base complexity</td><td>Standard</td><td>Large player bases can behave differently from untouched terrain; include one representative base before raising this control.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Animation quality</td><td>Standard</td><td>Provides a conservative state for busy settlements or multiplayer areas; raise only after those areas pass.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Motion blur</td><td>Off for comparison</td><td>Makes camera motion, scaling artifacts, and frame pacing easier to inspect. Restore later only by preference.</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
    <p class="muted">Menu names, presets, and available scaling options can change with major free updates. Photograph the current menu and use the nearest normal in-game setting. If a named option is absent, do not install an unofficial substitute just to reproduce this table.</p>

    <h2>Run a repeatable planet-to-space test</h2>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>Finish updates and restart.</strong> Complete the game, Windows, Lenovo firmware/software, intended graphics driver, and Legion Space updates before recording a baseline.</li>
      <li><strong>Record the full device state.</strong> Note game version, save, planet/location, driver, firmware, Legion Space version, power mode, charger, resolution, refresh, cap, scaling mode, and multiplayer state.</li>
      <li><strong>Walk a dense surface route twice.</strong> Include terrain generation, flora, fauna, structures, mining effects, inventory use, and weather if practical.</li>
      <li><strong>Fly low over the same area.</strong> Fast surface traversal can expose terrain and asset streaming that a static base view misses.</li>
      <li><strong>Leave the atmosphere.</strong> Include the transition, pulse flight, a station or freighter interior, and a short combat encounter when available.</li>
      <li><strong>Test a representative base or settlement.</strong> A simple starter shelter is not a useful proxy for a dense build or populated settlement.</li>
      <li><strong>Change one control at a time.</strong> Compare 40 FPS, a clearer scaling mode, textures, then effects—repeating the complete route after each change.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Decide whether 30 or 40 FPS fits the save</h2>
    <div class="grid cols3">
      <section class="card"><span class="chip">Stable 30</span><h3>Keep the consistency profile</h3><p>If every segment feels even, save the exact settings and device state. Raise texture clarity or one effect before increasing the cap.</p></section>
      <section class="card"><span class="chip">Test 40</span><h3>Headroom survives the full route</h3><p>Change only the cap and repeat the same planet, base, flight, transition, and combat pass. Keep 40 only if the weakest segment remains acceptable.</p></section>
      <section class="card"><span class="chip">Diagnose</span><h3>Streaming or heavy-area misses remain</h3><p>Restore Standard, verify files and free space, close background work, and repeat. Lower planet/base complexity or volumetrics according to the failing scene.</p></section>
    </div>

    <h2>Fix common No Man's Sky problems on Legion Go</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Symptom</th><th>Check first</th><th>Next step</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Low flight or fast traversal hitches</td><td>Restore Standard planet, texture, and base settings; check free storage and background downloads</td><td>Restart and repeat the exact route before deciding whether the hitch is persistent</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Storms or clouds miss the cap</td><td>Confirm 800p and Standard volumetrics, shadows, reflections, and planet quality</td><td>Keep the 30 FPS cap, pause overlays/recording, and rerun the same weather route</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Large bases perform worse</td><td>Return base complexity and animation quality to Standard</td><td>Test the same base offline/single-player only as a diagnostic, then restore the intended multiplayer state</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Image is too soft or shimmers</td><td>Confirm only one scaling method is active</td><td>Compare a clearer in-game quality mode at 800p before raising output resolution</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Camera movement feels uneven</td><td>Confirm a single frame cap and recorded refresh mode</td><td>Remove overlapping game, driver, and overlay caps; then retest without recording</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Controller prompts or inputs are wrong</td><td>Set Legion Space controls to gamepad mode</td><td>Restore default Steam Input and in-game controller settings before creating a custom layout</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Performance changed after an update</td><td>Restart and restore the photographed baseline</td><td>Confirm versions, verify files, and check Hello Games' official release log before unofficial edits</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Docked play is slower</td><td>Retest on the handheld screen with the charger connected directly</td><td>Check dock power and display output separately; do not default to native 4K rendering</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Storage, multiplayer, battery, and dock planning</h2>
    <p>Steam currently lists <strong>15GB of available space</strong>, Windows 10/11 64-bit, 8GB minimum memory, multiplayer, online co-op, cross-platform multiplayer, Steam Cloud, and full controller support. Leave room beyond 15GB for free updates, shader data, saves, screenshots, clips, and Windows temporary files. Use the <a href="/calculators/storage-planner/">storage planner</a>, then compare the <a href="/guides/microsd-vs-ssd-handheld-pc/">microSD-versus-SSD tradeoffs</a>.</p>
    <p>This page does not invent battery runtime. Planet, weather, base, multiplayer state, brightness, radios, power mode, cap, battery health, and thermals all change total draw. Measure your own complete route on the intended battery profile and use the <a href="/calculators/battery-estimator/">battery estimator</a>.</p>
    <p>Launch the intended save and verify online/offline behavior before travel. For TV play, stabilize the handheld profile first, then follow the <a href="/guides/handheld-gaming-usb-c-dock-checklist/">USB-C dock checklist</a>. A 4K desktop signal does not mean the game should render internally at 4K.</p>

    <h2>Optional gear after the profile is stable</h2>
    <p class="affiliate-note">Disclosure: these are broad Amazon searches marked sponsored/nofollow, not hands-on endorsements. Compare exact specifications, model fit, seller traceability, warranty, and return terms. No price, compatibility, performance, or battery claim is made; a real Associates tag is appended only when configured.</p>
    <div class="grid cols3">
      <a class="card gear-card" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=legion+go+a2+u3+microsd+card" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored" data-affiliate-link data-category="microsd-cards"><span class="chip">Sponsored search</span><h3>A2 / U3 microSD cards</h3><p class="muted">Compare capacity, seller traceability, warranty, and card-verification tools while leaving room for future updates.</p></a>
      <a class="card gear-card" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=legion+go+65w+usb+c+pd+charger" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored" data-affiliate-link data-category="chargers"><span class="chip">Sponsored search</span><h3>65W-class USB-C PD chargers</h3><p class="muted">Verify dedicated-port output, cable rating, port-sharing behavior, warranty, and exact-device support.</p></a>
      <a class="card gear-card" href="https://www.amazon.com/s?k=legion+go+usb+c+pd+dock+65w" target="_blank" rel="nofollow sponsored" data-affiliate-link data-category="docks"><span class="chip">Sponsored search</span><h3>Legion Go USB-C docks</h3><p class="muted">Check PD passthrough, display modes, host-cable reach, physical clearance, and support for the exact model.</p></a>
    </div>
    <p>Compare categories in the <a href="/gear/">spec-based gear library</a>, use the <a href="/guides/legion-go-accessories-buying-checklist/">Legion Go accessory buying checklist</a>, or set a limit with the <a href="/calculators/accessory-budget/">accessory budget calculator</a>.</p>

    <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
    <div class="grid cols2">
      {faqs.map(faq => <section class="card"><h3>{faq.question}</h3><p>{faq.answer}</p></section>)}
    </div>

    <h2>Sources and methodology</h2>
    <p>Sources were checked on August 16, 2026. Steam's live store data supplied the August 12, 2016 release date, current 15GB storage requirement, minimum PC context, multiplayer/co-op and Steam Cloud labels, full-controller-support label, Hello Games identity, and official image. Hello Games supplies the official site and update log. Lenovo PSREF supplies the original Legion Go product route and device-family context.</p>
    <p>The settings are a conservative editorial test sequence derived from those public constraints and normal graphics-diagnosis practice. Handheld Settings Lab did not personally benchmark the current game, procedural world, save, Windows build, driver, firmware, Legion Space version, battery, thermals, or multiplayer session. The 30 and 40 FPS figures are test targets, not measured guarantees; no search-volume or fixed-runtime claim is made.</p>
    <ul>{sources.map(source => <li><a href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="nofollow noopener">{source.label}</a></li>)}</ul>
    <p>Return to the <a href="/legion-go-settings/">Legion Go settings hub</a>, compare the general <a href="/steam-deck-settings/no-mans-sky/">Steam Deck</a> and <a href="/rog-ally-settings/no-mans-sky/">ROG Ally</a> pages, or use the <a href="/calculators/">battery, storage, and accessory calculators</a> with your own observations.</p>
  </article>
</Base>
